Here's how to save and restore draft text using Window lifecycle events:

**App.xaml.cs** — Override `CreateWindow` and hook `Stopped`/`Resumed`/`Destroying`:

```csharp
public partial class App : Application
{
    protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
    {
        var window = base.CreateWindow(activationState);

        window.Stopped += (s, e) => SaveDraft();
        window.Resumed += (s, e) => RestoreDraft();
        window.Destroying += (s, e) => SaveDraft(); // Android back-button skips Stopped

        return window;
    }

    private void SaveDraft()
    {
        if (Shell.Current?.CurrentPage is NotePage page)
        {
            Preferences.Set("draft_text", page.ViewModel.DraftText);
        }
    }

    private void RestoreDraft()
    {
        if (Shell.Current?.CurrentPage is NotePage page)
        {
            page.ViewModel.DraftText = Preferences.Get("draft_text", string.Empty);
        }
    }
}
```

**NoteViewModel.cs**:

```csharp
public partial class NoteViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    [ObservableProperty]
    private string _draftText = string.Empty;
}
```

**NotePage.xaml.cs** — restore on first appearance too:

```csharp
public partial class NotePage : ContentPage
{
    public NoteViewModel ViewModel { get; }

    public NotePage(NoteViewModel vm)
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        ViewModel = vm;
        BindingContext = vm;

        // Restore any saved draft on page load
        vm.DraftText = Preferences.Get("draft_text", string.Empty);
    }
}
```

### Key points

| Concern | Approach |
|---------|----------|
| Save on background | `Window.Stopped` event |
| Restore on resume | `Window.Resumed` event |
| Android back-button | Also save in `Window.Destroying` (skips Stopped) |
| Storage | `Preferences` — fast, synchronous, no ANR risk |
| First launch | `Resumed` doesn't fire initially, so restore in the page constructor |

Keep handlers fast (< 1–2 seconds) to avoid ANR on Android or watchdog kills on iOS. `Preferences` is ideal for small string values like draft text.
